{%- comment -%}
  Zaria — the one definition of the main rail, read by both the desktop header and the mobile
  drawer. Shopify's navigation sits behind a scope this store's custom app does not hold, so
  the menu cannot be edited in the admin by anything but a person; rather than leave the rail
  hostage to that, it is written here and the admin's Main menu is no longer read.

  Structure asked for by the client, 2026-11-13:
      New In · Designers · Categories · Ready to Wear · Made to Order · Sales

  One row per item, fields separated by ~ and rows by ||
      key ~ label ~ href ~ kind
  kind is one of
      link  a plain word in the rail
      drop  a short dropdown list        (snippets/zaria-nav-panel, zaria-nav-sub)
      mega  a full-width panel of columns
      sale  a plain word in the house colour
  The children of every drop/mega live in zaria-nav-panel (desktop) and zaria-nav-sub (mobile);
  adding a designer or a category means editing those two and this list, nothing else.
{%- endcomment -%}
new-in        ~ New In        ~ {{ routes.root_url }}collections/new                ~ link ||
designers     ~ Designers     ~ {{ routes.root_url }}collections/ready-to-wear      ~ drop ||
categories    ~ Categories    ~ {{ routes.root_url }}collections/all               ~ drop ||
ready-to-wear ~ Ready to Wear  ~ {{ routes.root_url }}collections/ready-to-wear      ~ drop ||
made-to-order ~ Made to Order ~ {{ routes.root_url }}pages/design-your-look         ~ drop ||
sales         ~ Sales         ~ {{ routes.root_url }}collections/sale               ~ sale
